      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THE NIGHT FOX NZ (5) is an ex NZ trained gelding who resumes from a spell after finishing fourth at his latest appearance at Cambridge Raceway on April 2. Has won once and placed twice from his four previous runs. Fresh-up has winning claims. WICKED MITZI (2) turned in a much better run last time out, finishing second over 1690m at Kilmore after getting checked over the final stages. Has the benefit of a good draw. It doesn't get any easier but she is good enough to take this out. OUR ULTIMATE GRACY NZ (3) is on the radar after her last-start fifth over 1720m at Melton a week-and-a-half ago. Rates well as an each-way chance. IN AN IDEAL WORLD (8) is worth some thought after his last-start sixth over 1720m at Melton on August 12 after he raced outside the leader at the bell.",
